  writeup: "PAYNE-LAB-17 made 160 connections to 40 hosts on ports 22/80/443/3389 in three minutes at 15:41. Every connection is S0 or REJ with zero bytes: a network scan (T1046) where nothing connected. The account is sestun@pupils.payneschool.example, a pupil, signed in interactively at 15:38; the class calendar shows cyber club in that lab until 15:35; the EDR shows an open-source scanner run from a USB stick, no install, no internet traffic. Reading: a curious pupil, not an attacker. Escalated to the school as a safeguarding and conduct matter with the facts. Could not be confirmed: nothing further \u2014 no host was accessed.",
